;;; Written for this review: a relation named ONLY by an activator. `happy` is
;;; written in no declaration, no fact's head, no fact's argument and no
;;; rule's text: only as the argument of `(tag happy)`, where `tag`'s
;;; parameter ?R heads its conclusion. The rule concludes (happy Ann) all the
;;; same. A goal over `happy` loads, since the goal check counts a name passed
;;; where a relation's name is held (Q-M1f.114's "a name a fact or a conclusion
;;; passes where a relation's name is held").

(relation person P :why "{?1} is a person")

(person Ann)

(rule tag (?R)
  :match  (person ?x)
  :assert (?R ?x)
  :why    "every person is {?R}")

(tag happy)

(solve :no-search)
(query :goal (happy ?x)
  :expect (model (happy Ann)))
